{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He blessed them</b> — He implanted in them the power of generation, to be blessed forever with many sons and daughters. The intent is to say that procreation comes from the blessing of Elohim, for they were not born but were created from nothing and blessed to do thus." "And the reason for <b>And He called their name Adam</b> is that the name אדם is a general term for the entire human species, so Scripture notes that Elohim called the first pair by this name, because all of them were potentially contained within them, and concerning them He says, \"This is the book of the generations of Adam\" (Genesis 5:1). And our master Sherira Gaon wrote that the Sages transmitted to one another, by oral tradition and by the arrangement of markings, some of which are expounded in the order of the verse \"This is the book of the generations of Adam,\" and some in the order of the verse after it, \"Male and female He created them\" — and the secrets of the Torah and the mysteries are not transmitted except to one in whom they see signs that he is worthy of that. These are the words of the Gaon, and we have not merited them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The phrase הכרת פנים is translated literally as 'recognition of faces,' i.e., oral tradition conveyed face to face; סדרי שרטוטין, literally 'arrangements of drawings/markings,' is rendered literally as the technical sense is uncertain. The final phrase ולא זכינו בהם is rendered hyper-literally as 'we have not merited them.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:53.656365188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}